    <item>
      <title>Breakfast Wrap: Intergenerational Report's focus on who we are and where we're going</title>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Is Australia prepared for the challenges in the decades ahead for the nation? The federal government has just released the latest Intergenerational Report which shows how an aging population is expected to reshape the economy in the next 40 years. The report predicts that for the first time, deaths will outpace births in Australia by the mid 2060s. As the number of tax-paying Australians potential shrinks, the next four decades will see successive budget deficits. This comes as a Senate Inquiry has delivered 11 recommendations in the wake of last year's massive Optus Triple-Zero outage, which has been linked to two deaths.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <link>https://www.abc.net.au/listen/programs/radionational-breakfast/radio-national-breakfast/107109522</link>
